{
  "dom_id": "step-q89802",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{1-x}-1?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's re-write the expression, as follows:\n\n$$\ny=-\\sqrt{1-x}-1=-\\sqrt{-(x-1)}-1\n$$\n\nTo get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{-(x-1)}-1,$ we can do the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Reflect the graph in the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{-x}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/712c0945824e8d1b2a1d4f6b87c1d7d2adb1b9db572509e497a60b2eeaa81127.png)\n\n- Reflect the graph in the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{-x}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/2505d3dba2e7d90a72447bb80c01553dca95cfa0470156fb610b8b317ce99089.png)\n\n- Translate the result to the right by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{-(x-1)}.$\n\n- Translate the result down by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{-(x-1)}-1.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/08c1533b04a800b95f2160c51a9ef5a8ebcabd1156a5a788c509d19d2a5f6c8b.png)",
